## The idea

Evict the key used **least often**; among keys used equally often, the one used **least recently**. Group keys into **buckets by use count**. Each bucket is a LinkedList with the most recent at the front, so the back of the lowest bucket is the victim. Keep **minFreq**, the lowest count that has a bucket, so finding the victim is O(1). For GetRank, each entry also stores a **"last used" tick**; rank = 1 + the number of entries that would outlive it (higher count, or same count and used more recently).

## Step by step

1. Entry: key, value, frequency, last-used tick, and its node in its bucket list.
2. Use(entry): remove it from its bucket (delete the bucket if empty; if that was minFreq, minFreq goes up by one). Frequency++, put it at the front of the new bucket, tick++.
3. TryGet: missing → false. Otherwise Use(entry) and return the value.
4. Put existing key: update the value and Use(entry).
5. Put new key: if full, remove the back of bucket[minFreq] (least recently used among the least frequent). Then add the new entry with frequency 1 at the front of bucket 1, and minFreq = 1.
6. GetRank(key): missing → −1. Otherwise count the entries with a higher frequency, or the same frequency and a later tick. Rank = that count + 1. It does not call Use, so it does not count as a use.

## Worked example

**Input:** capacity 3: Put a, b, c; Get a, Get a, Get b; then Put d

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| Put a, b, c | bucket 1: [c, b, a]; minFreq 1 |
| Get a ×2 | a moves to bucket 2, then bucket 3 |
| Get b | b moves to bucket 2; bucket 1: [c] |
| GetRank | a: nobody above → 1; b: a above → 2; c: a and b above → 3 |
| Put d | full → victim is the back of bucket[minFreq = 1] → c |
| after | bucket 1: [d], minFreq 1 |

**Result:** c is evicted; a and b survive

## Cost

TryGet and Put are O(1). GetRank is O(n) because it compares against every entry — simple and correct; a faster rank needs an order-statistics structure (see follow-ups). Memory O(capacity).

## The code (C#, compiled and tested against every part of the question)

```csharp
// Evict the least frequently used key; among equal frequencies, the least recently used.
public sealed class LfuRankCache<TKey, TValue> {
    private class Entry {
        public TKey Key;
        public TValue Value;
        public int Freq;                         // how many times it was used
        public long LastUse;                     // larger = used more recently
        public LinkedListNode<Entry> Node;       // where it sits in its bucket
    }

    private readonly int _capacity;
    private readonly Dictionary<TKey, Entry> _entries = new Dictionary<TKey, Entry>();
    // frequency -> keys with that frequency, most recently used at the front
    private readonly Dictionary<int, LinkedList<Entry>> _buckets = new Dictionary<int, LinkedList<Entry>>();
    private int _minFreq = 0;
    private long _tick = 0;

    public LfuRankCache(int capacity) {
        if (capacity <= 0) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(nameof(capacity));
        _capacity = capacity;
    }

    public int Count {
        get { return _entries.Count; }
    }

    public bool TryGet(TKey key, out TValue value) {
        Entry e;
        if (!_entries.TryGetValue(key, out e)) {
            value = default;
            return false;
        }
        Use(e);
        value = e.Value;
        return true;
    }

    public void Put(TKey key, TValue value) {
        Entry e;
        if (_entries.TryGetValue(key, out e)) {
            e.Value = value;
            Use(e);
            return;
        }

        if (_entries.Count == _capacity) {
            // Least frequent bucket; its back is the least recently used in it.
            LinkedList<Entry> bucket = _buckets[_minFreq];
            Entry victim = bucket.Last.Value;
            bucket.RemoveLast();
            if (bucket.Count == 0) _buckets.Remove(_minFreq);
            _entries.Remove(victim.Key);
        }

        e = new Entry();
        e.Key = key;
        e.Value = value;
        e.Freq = 1;
        _tick++;
        e.LastUse = _tick;
        e.Node = BucketFor(1).AddFirst(e);
        _entries[key] = e;
        _minFreq = 1;                            // a new key always has the lowest frequency
    }

    // 1 = the entry that would be evicted last. Reading the rank is not a use.
    public int GetRank(TKey key) {
        Entry me;
        if (!_entries.TryGetValue(key, out me)) return -1;

        int better = 0;
        foreach (Entry other in _entries.Values) {
            if (other == me) continue;
            bool usedMore = other.Freq > me.Freq;
            bool sameButNewer = other.Freq == me.Freq && other.LastUse > me.LastUse;
            if (usedMore || sameButNewer) better++;
        }
        return better + 1;
    }

    // Move an entry from bucket f to bucket f + 1.
    private void Use(Entry e) {
        LinkedList<Entry> oldBucket = _buckets[e.Freq];
        oldBucket.Remove(e.Node);
        if (oldBucket.Count == 0) {
            _buckets.Remove(e.Freq);
            if (_minFreq == e.Freq) _minFreq = e.Freq + 1;   // e is moving there, so it exists
        }

        e.Freq++;
        _tick++;
        e.LastUse = _tick;
        e.Node = BucketFor(e.Freq).AddFirst(e);
    }

    private LinkedList<Entry> BucketFor(int freq) {
        LinkedList<Entry> bucket;
        if (!_buckets.TryGetValue(freq, out bucket)) {
            bucket = new LinkedList<Entry>();
            _buckets[freq] = bucket;
        }
        return bucket;
    }
}
```

## Likely follow-up questions

**Q: GetRank on a missing key? Ties at the minimum frequency?**

−1; least recent loses

**Q: Complexity of GetRank — and of Get/Put given the sorted counts?**

O(F + B); O(log F)

**Q: Can GetRank be O(log n)?**

Order-statistics / Fenwick

**Q: Thread-safety — reader/writer lock?**

One lock; Get writes, so RW does not help

**Q: Millions of keys; frequencies grow forever.**

Aging (halve periodically) or W-TinyLFU

**Q: How would you know the cache has fossilised?**

Age of evicted entries, hit ratio on new keys

